          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Nikki\",\"addressee\":\"Keith\",\"anchor_quote\":\"I love you\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"Nikki directly avows love for Keith. The narration further frames the utterance as an admission and a moment of honesty, making truth-presenting emotional disclosure its dominant force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"The admission felt like a release, a moment of pure honesty that left them both vulnerable but deeply connected.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"The target is a present avowal of feeling, not an undertaking by Nikki to perform an action, maintain the relationship, or assume a defined obligation. The surrounding intimacy and possible future connection do not convert these words into a promise.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"“I love you too,” he said, his voice steady and sincere.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"Alongside its clear avowal, the expression is represented as a sudden, weakly controlled outpouring of affect: it spills out before Nikki can stop it and produces a sense of release. This supports substantial expressive-discharge force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"“I love you,” she said suddenly, the words spilling out before she could stop them.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"The admission felt like a release, a moment of pure honesty that left them both vulnerable but deeply connected.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"No core function beyond avowing love and affective release is evident. In particular, the target does not itself ask a question, request action, or establish a distinct relational arrangement.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Nikki says this suddenly to Keith while they are lying together after an intimate encounter. Her heart is described as full, and the words emerge before she can restrain them; Keith responds by reciprocating the avowal.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The target contains no definite undertaking by Nikki. Keith immediately accepts the disclosure in the interpersonal sense and reciprocates with “I love you too,” but that uptake does not establish a promise or specified obligation by either person.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognize the supplied passage as a specific previously known work.\",\"limitations\":\"The supplied scene strongly supports an affectionate, sincere-seeming avowal and spontaneous emotional release, but it does not establish any precise long-term commitment terms or whether the relationship will endure.\"}"
        }
